%% Refresh-token rotation with reuse detection — the most interesting mechanism in ClubHub,
%% and one the original AWS diagram never drew. Contract: docs/adr/0002-auth-token-contract.md.
%% Deployment-independent: this behaves identically on Fargate and on the droplet.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as Browser
    participant F as Frontend<br/>(axios client)
    participant A as API<br/>(/auth/*)
    participant D as Postgres<br/>(refresh_tokens)

    Note over U,D: Login — one access token in the body, one opaque refresh token in a cookie

    U->>F: submit credentials
    F->>A: POST /auth/login
    A->>D: INSERT refresh_tokens (sha256 hash, expires_at +30d)
    A-->>F: 200 { access_token }  +  Set-Cookie: clubhub_refresh<br/>HttpOnly · Secure · SameSite=Lax · Path=/auth
    Note right of F: access token held IN MEMORY only<br/>(never localStorage)

    Note over U,D: 15 minutes later — the access token expires

    F->>A: GET /clubs/my (Bearer, expired)
    A-->>F: 401
    Note right of F: interceptor single-flights the refresh<br/>so N parallel 401s cause ONE rotate
    F->>A: POST /auth/refresh (cookie sent automatically)
    A->>D: SELECT by token_hash
    D-->>A: row: revoked_at IS NULL, not expired
    A->>D: UPDATE old SET revoked_at = now()<br/>INSERT new token
    A-->>F: 200 { access_token } + Set-Cookie (rotated)
    F->>A: retry the original request
    A-->>F: 200

    Note over U,D: Attack — a stolen token is replayed after it was rotated

    rect rgb(253, 236, 234)
        U->>A: POST /auth/refresh (OLD, already-revoked token)
        A->>D: SELECT by token_hash
        D-->>A: row found, revoked_at IS NOT NULL
        Note right of A: revoked_at is checked BEFORE expires_at.<br/>A revoked row must therefore outlive the<br/>token's validity for this branch to fire —<br/>which is why the prune job keeps 30d + 7d.
        A->>D: revoke ALL refresh tokens for this user
        A-->>U: 401 REFRESH_REUSED
        Note over U,D: every session for that user is now dead —<br/>the legitimate user is logged out too, by design
    end
